# Host logrotate conf for web.log and poller.log (installed to
# /etc/logrotate.d/magus-logs on the VPS — see docs/1-deploy/docker.md).
#
# Only these two files, never a glob: caddy.log rotates itself (see the
# Caddyfile's own log block) and two rotators fighting over one file
# corrupts or loses data.
#
# copytruncate is mandatory, not a style choice: web and poller hold one
# open file descriptor to their log for their whole process lifetime (a
# plain shell redirect gives them no signal to reopen it), so a rename-based
# rotation would make their output invisible until the next restart.
# copytruncate keeps the same inode open and truncates it in place instead.
# Accepted cost: a log line written between the copy and the truncate can be
# lost — a fair trade for a log file, not a data store.
/home/magus/magus-logs/web.log
/home/magus/magus-logs/poller.log
{
	daily
	rotate 14
	size 10M
	compress
	delaycompress
	copytruncate
	missingok
	notifempty
}
